<title>UK: British trucks still stuck in Basque region.</title>
<headline>British trucks still stuck in Basque region.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>There are around 100 British drivers still blocked in the Basque region of Spain as the country's truckers continue their strike, Freight Transport Association (FTA) spokesman Greg Dossetter told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We are concerned for the drivers' personal safety as threats of intimidation are still continuing,&quot; he added. &quot;However things appear to be moving a lot better elsewhere in Spain with the Spanish authorities providing escorts,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Alan McLaughlin, spokesman for Tesco Plc said that hauliers working for the British supermarket chain &quot;are getting through on selected routes as long as these are carefully chosen&quot;. --Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44-171-542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
